            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitational+waves"} gravitational waves
            and/or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+waves"} electromagnetic waves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vector"} wave vector
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricci+flat"} Ricci flat
            pp-wave spacetimes are examples of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+spacetimes"} universal spacetimes
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsPenroseLimits As Penrose limits
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            looks like a pp-wave near a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lightlike"} lightlike
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
            %a{:href => "#Penrose76"} Penrose 1976
            and hence came to be called the
            %em Penrose limit
            (review includes
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Blau11"} Blau 11
          %p
            Notice that Penrose limits of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifolds"} Einstein manifolds
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricci+flat"} Ricci flat
            (
            %a{:href => "#Philip05"}> Philip 2005, Prop. 3.4.1
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Philip06"} Philip 2006, Prop. 3
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Blau11"} Blau 2011
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BlauPlaneWavesAndPenroseLimit.pdf#page=41"} p. 41
          %p#MaximallySupersymmetric11dExample
            For example, the Penrose limit of both the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            solution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_4 \times S^7
            as well as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            solution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7 \times S^4
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            are &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#BlauFigueroaHullPapadopoulos02"}> BFHP 2002
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#BerensteinMaldacenaNastase02"} BMN 2002, §2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kowalski-Glikman84"} Kowalski-Glikman 1984 (9)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FigueroaPapadopoulos01"} Figueroa-O’Farrill &amp; Papadopoulos 2001 (12,14)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MaximallySuSyWaveIn11D"} below
          %h3#relation_to_bmn_matrix_model Relation to BMN matrix model
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            (
            %a{:href => "#BerensteinMaldacenaNastase02"}> BMN 02, Section 5 and Appendix B
            ) is a deformation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            by
            = succeed "-terms" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            background to the maximally supersymmetric pp-wave (discussed
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MaximallySuSyWaveIn11D"} below
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#MaximallySuSyWaveIn11D Maximally supersymmetric pp-wave in 11d
          %p
